# Environments — author here, build and flash there

| | Workstation (this workspace) | Heliotrope Ridge (build host) |
|---|---|---|
| Role | Author code, docs, git, `gh` | Compile, flash, serial capture, soak |
| PlatformIO / device on USB | **absent** — `$HOME` is read-only, never install toolchains here | `/opt/homebrew/bin/pio`, the only machine with the RAK4631 |
| Repo path | here | `~/Documents/GitHub/lorawan/rak-sensor-node-but-better` |

**The build host is the operator's laptop and moves between networks.** A failed SSH means the
laptop is elsewhere — ask for the address; do not investigate a "dead host". No address is in
the repo (it is public): scripts resolve `BUILD_HOST`, then `RAK_BUILD_HOST`, then the first
line of the untracked `~/.rak-build-host`, and fail by name if none is set. Verify with
`ssh -o ConnectTimeout=8 -o BatchMode=yes "$RAK_BUILD_HOST" 'zsh -l -c "hostname"'` →
`Heliotrope-Ridge`. Never paste the address into anything tracked; `scripts/preflight.sh`
fails on IPv4 literals.

**The SSH gotcha:** non-interactive SSH skips `~/.zprofile`, so `pio` looks uninstalled. Always
`zsh -l -c "..."`, or better, use `scripts/remote.sh`, which handles the login shell, the `cd`,
and the sentinels.

**Git is the only transport.** Never `scp`/`rsync`/paste between machines. Before any remote
build: commit and push locally, `pull --ff-only` on the build host, confirm its HEAD equals the
SHA you intend to build, and report that SHA. `scripts/remote.sh sync` does this and refuses a
dirty remote tree. If the build host has local commits, surface it; never rebase or discard the
operator's work.

**Two GitHub identities, both normal.** The workstation's HTTPS credential helper and `gh` are
`disruptivepatternmaterial` and **can push** (re-verified 2026-08-28; confirm with
`git push --dry-run origin HEAD:refs/heads/main`). The SSH keys are the work account and 403 —
do not "fix" the remote URL. Commits you did not write appear on `origin/main` because the
operator pushes from their IDE, sometimes capturing an agent's in-progress tree: fetch, look,
fix forward, never rewrite pushed history. `scripts/push.sh` remains as a relay via the build
host and guards against pushing during a soak.

**Every build, flash, or soak result names its host and commit SHA** — otherwise it is not
evidence (`docs/EVIDENCE.md`). Full detail: `docs/ENVIRONMENTS.md`.
